Today is Saturday morning.
I am in the park with Asha's dog.
Moti is very happy.
We walk slowly.
Suddenly, he sees a squirrel.
The squirrel is near a tree.
Moti runs forward fast.
He pulls the leash hard.
I also hold the leash tightly.
Asha's rule is clear.
In the park, I must never let go of the leash.
Therefore, I pull him back.
I say, "Moti, come here!"
"You must not go there!"
"You must not run, stay here!"
He comes near me.
I command him, "Sit on the ground!"
He sits on the ground.
I pet him affectionately, and he becomes calm.
Then we walk slowly again.
